## Critical Context
- `end_crossed` boolean tracks the first crossing of `end_at` to set `ballots_at_end` exactly once
- `submit_ballot` guard requires `is_voting()` (`start_at <= time < end_at`) and `voter.in(candidate_set)`
- `enclave_tally` guard requires `is_tallying()` and `not(enclave_has_session_key)`; it honestly computes `tally_spec(ballots, candidates)`
- `publish_result` guard requires `is_tallying()` and `enclave_computed_tally.present`
- B10 cross-layer property modeled as classical shadow: `tally_result.value == enclave_computed_tally.value ∧ enclave_consumed_ballots == ballots_at_end`
- Witness invariants are negations: `not(tally_result.present)`, `not(ballots.keys().size() > 0)`, `not(end_crossed)`

